{
  "slug": "murray-road-column-cladding-case-study-from-inquiry-to-acceptance",
  "title": "From Inquiry to Acceptance: The Murray Road Column Cladding Case Study, Hong Kong, China — A Sculptural Double-Curved Column in 16 Stages, from Site Survey and Shop Drawings to Factory Mock-Up, Export Packing and Signed Handover",
  "excerpt": "A complete metalwork case study from first inquiry to signed acceptance: how a sculptural double-curved, lobed column cladding was delivered for a prime address on Murray Road, Central, Hong Kong, China. Sixteen documented stages — inquiry and design briefing, site survey, shop drawings and flat patterns, sealed sample approval, inbound material inspection, cutting and curve forming to radius templates, pair-wise trial fit, a full-scale factory mock-up of the whole column with a walkthrough video, the internal ring-frame substructure with adjustable fixings, continuous seam welding and dressing, surface finishing and factory inspection, export packing in fitted plywood crates, container loading, site installation as alignment rather than fabrication, client acceptance under raking light, and the aftercare routine — documented with 42 project photographs and one factory video, exactly as the work happened.",
